From 835aefc5611239c1bdee744fcadcf5ab2bc353b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavier Ruiz <github@xav.ie>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:28:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Keep apps named in EXECUTOR_SEARCH_EXCLUDE_APPS out of
 searches without a namespace

The local server reads EXECUTOR_SEARCH_EXCLUDE_APPS, a comma separated list of
app slugs, and passes it to makeMcp as the searchExcludedApps option. Searches
without a namespace (the search tool, tools.search and CodeMode's global
search()) leave those apps out, so apps that only re-export other apps' tools do
not crowd results. A search in one of their namespaces still finds their tools.
The MCP package reads no environment; without the option nothing is excluded.
